    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Large Detached country home of over 2,800 sq ft with beautifully landscaped gardens and enjoying far reaching views from an elevated position would make for an ideal family home. An early viewing is recommended.\n\nThis beautifully presented three-bedroom detached property is situated in the peaceful rural setting of Tullyhoner, Breenagh, Co. Donegal, and enjoys beautiful views over the surrounding countryside. The property is exceptionally well maintained throughout and offers bright, spacious and comfortable living.\n\nInternally, the accommodation comprises of three bedrooms, four bathrooms (three of which are ensuite), sitting room, dining room, kitchen, sunroom and a large utility room. The sunroom provides an ideal space to relax and enjoy the attractive views and surrounding landscape. The property also benefits from an excellent BER B energy rating.\n\nExternally, the property is a real standout, with the grounds extensively landscaped and meticulously maintained. A number of beautiful feature points throughout the gardens add to the property`s unique character and appeal. To the rear is a particularly attractive rockery, complemented by a decorative stone wall surrounding the rear of the property.\n\nThe property also benefits from a substantial detached garage/workshop measuring approximately 18ft x 26ft. This versatile space is fitted with a wash hand basin and toilet and features extensive plumbing and electrical points, together with an electric roller door.\n\nCombining excellent accommodation, stunning countryside views and beautifully landscaped grounds, this is a wonderful turnkey property that offers a peaceful setting together with generous and highly practical additional space.\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this unique property has to offer.\n\n---\n\nPaved steps lead to a partially glazed PVC front door.\n\nEntrance Hallway: 17.4 x 14 ft, with decorative tiled flooring, a feature stone-built column and a decorative staircase.\n\nSitting Room: 14.3 x 19.9 ft, leading to a bay window, with solid oak flooring, and coving and cornicing to the ceiling. Features a gas fireplace, with a decorative cast iron surround. This room enjoys beautiful views over the surrounding countryside. \n\nKitchen: 18.1 x 14.4 ft, with decorative tiled flooring, and a stone feature wall. Extensive built-in wall and base solid oak kitchen units, with a tiled surround, an integrated fridge-freezer, and an integrated dishwasher. Double sink and drainer unit, with mixer taps over. Large island unit with a granite worktop, a cooker point and an extractor hood over. \n\nDining Area: 16.7 x 14.5 ft, leading to bay window, with tiled flooring, and coving and cornicing to the ceiling. Features an inset solid fuel stove with a decorative stone surround. This room also benefits from spectacular countryside views.\n\nSunroom: 17 x 13 ft, with solid oak flooring, and a pine tongue and groove, vaulted ceiling. Features a solid fuel stove with a back boiler set on a slate plinth, with a decorative stone surround. Glazed double French doors lead to the rear. \n\nUtility Room: Tiled flooring, and built-in wall and base storage units providing ample storage, with a tiled surround. Stainless steel single sink and drainer unit. Plumbed for washing machine and wired for tumble dryer. A partially glazed PVC door leads to the rear.\n\nBedroom Three (Downstairs): 14.5 x 12 ft, with timber flooring.\n\nEnsuite: Tiled flooring, fully tiled walls, with a white two-piece suite. Double shower cubicle with glass shower doors, containing an Aqualisa shower.\nMain Bathroom: 10.6 x 8.9 ft, with tiled flooring, fully tiled walls, and a white three-piece suite.\n\nA solid oak staircase with carpet flooring, leads to the first floor.\n\nBedroom One: 22.3 x 14.6 ft, with timber flooring and a walk-in wardrobe providing extensive shelving and handing space. This bedroom overlooks uninterrupted countryside views.\n\nEnsuite: Tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, with a white two-piece suite. A fully tiled separate shower cubicle, with glass shower enclosure, contains a Triton T90 electric shower.\n\nBedroom Two: 19.4 x 14.4 ft, with timber flooring, and a walk-in wardrobe providing extensive hanging and shelving space.\n\nEnsuite: Tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, with a white two-piece suite. A fully tiled separate shower cubicle, with glass shower doors contains an Aqualisa power shower.\n\nOutside: Stone entrance walls with electric gates, lead to a tarmac driveway surrounding the house, providing ample parking. The front garden is laid to lawn, with mature hedging to the boundaries. The property is extensively landscaped, with many beautiful feature points, which make this property particularly unique. To the rear, is a meticulously presented rockery, with a decorative stone wall surrounding the rear of the property. There is also a detached garage / workshop, measuring at 18 x 26 ft, which features a wash hand basin, toilet, extensive plumbing and electrical points, and an electric roller door.\n\nDisclaimer - The above particulars are issued by Glen Estates on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through them. Information contained in the brochure does not form any part of any offer or contract and is provided in good faith, for guidance only. Glen estates have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. Maps and plans are not to scale and measurements are approximate, photographs provided for guidance only. The particulars, descriptions, dimensions, references to condition, permissions or licences for use or occupation, access and any other details, such as prices, rents or any other outgoings are for guidance only and may be subject to change. Intending purchasers / tenants must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of details provided to them either verbally or as part of this brochure. Neither Glen Estates or any of its employees have any authority to make or give any representation or warranty in respect of this property.\n"
      },
